Add a style class to Fractal's window so user CSS can target it.

GTK adds no app-identifying style class to windows, and libadwaita apps
ignore GTK themes, so ~/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css is the only place to style
them -- but it applies to every app at once. Nautilus tags its own window
with .nautilus-window; Fractal tags nothing, so there is no way to scope
rules (such as the translucent sidebar in modules/home/wlroots/gtk.nix) to
it. Add the equivalent class here.

--- a/src/window.blp
+++ b/src/window.blp
@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@ template $Window: Adw.ApplicationWindow {
   height-request: 294;
   title: _("Fractal");
 
+  styles [
+    "fractal-window",
+  ]
+
   content: Adw.ToastOverlay toast_overlay {
     Gtk.Stack main_stack {
       transition-type: crossfade;
